// Lake City (docs/SCENARIOS.md, docs/LAYOUTS.md): a flat grid city of the 1980s on a great lake,
// built to work and warm inside, on a real great-lakes city's north and west sides at about
// 200 m to the mile: the mile-line streets, the old diagonal trails cutting north-west, the
// expressways, the shore drive through the lakefront park, the river forking beside
// downtown, the inner suburbs past the north limits, and the drive-in on the plank road
// near the north-west corner. Every road ends on another road.
//
// The sections between `realmap` markers are generated from public-domain US Census
// TIGER/Line 2023 roads and USGS 3DEP elevation by `tools/realmap` (import:
// tools/realmap/lake_city.ron); edit that file and rerun it, not these sections. Road names
// are invented.
//
// Meters, x east, z south, (0, 0) the north-west corner; 16 x 16 chunks, 2048 m square.
